repository-code: "https://github.com/Urban-Meteorology-Reading/STEBBSv2-Evaluation"
abstract: >-
  Python scripts, Jupyter notebooks, and supporting data for site parameter
  derivation, model evaluation, and visualisation accompanying the study
  "Building energy modelling for urban weather and climate studies: STEBBS v2.0".
  The repository includes characterisation of the BRTYND site in Bristol,
  evaluation of SUEWS-STEBBS and EnergyPlus simulations against indoor
  observations, and evaluation of solar radiation splitting methods for
  Bristol and Berlin. Model input and output files are archived separately
  at https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23955440. See README.md for dependencies,
  external-data requirements, and data availability.
keywords:
  - STEBBS
  - SUEWS
  - EnergyPlus
  - urban climate
  - building energy modelling
  - model evaluation
